# Production build settings, picked up automatically by `vite build` (and so by
# `npm run tauri build`, whose beforeBuildCommand is `npm run build`).
#
# The gateway serves the shared read-only feeds — model benchmarks, the MCP
# directory, Hugging Face search — so a release works out of the box with no API
# key of the user's own. Only the web build used to get this, because
# deploy/webapp.sh passes it explicitly; desktop installers shipped without it and
# fell back to demanding the user's own Artificial Analysis key, which made the
# Benchmarks view fail with a 401 on a fresh install.
#
# Dev builds deliberately do NOT load this file (Vite reads .env.development in
# dev), so `npm run dev` keeps calling the services directly, as gateway.ts
# describes. A user can still override it in Settings → server URL.
VITE_GATEWAY_URL=https://hsapi.retris.io
